WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:00.998
Fill it with

00:00:00.810 --> 00:00:02.295
paint never paint

00:00:02.107 --> 00:00:02.531
it

00:00:03.054 --> 00:00:03.867
Take the curve

00:00:03.679 --> 00:00:04.681
y equals one

00:00:04.493 --> 00:00:05.247
over x

00:00:05.412 --> 00:00:06.237
start at x

00:00:06.049 --> 00:00:06.910
equals one

00:00:07.004 --> 00:00:07.794
and spin it

00:00:07.606 --> 00:00:08.761
around the axis

00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:09.489
You get a

00:00:09.301 --> 00:00:10.504
horn that narrows

00:00:10.315 --> 00:00:11.081
forever

00:00:11.614 --> 00:00:12.604
Its volume is

00:00:12.416 --> 00:00:13.477
exactly pi

00:00:13.513 --> 00:00:14.585
just over three

00:00:14.397 --> 00:00:15.352
cubic units

00:00:15.388 --> 00:00:16.272
yet its surface

00:00:16.083 --> 00:00:17.356
area is infinite

00:00:17.496 --> 00:00:18.604
A finite tin

00:00:18.415 --> 00:00:19.311
fills it but

00:00:19.123 --> 00:00:20.160
no amount paints

00:00:19.972 --> 00:00:20.408
it

00:00:20.942 --> 00:00:22.416
Known as Torricelli's

00:00:22.227 --> 00:00:22.923
trumpet

00:00:23.112 --> 00:00:24.267
the paradox has

00:00:24.185 --> 00:00:25.446
unsettled people for

00:00:25.258 --> 00:00:26.791
nearly four centuries

00:00:26.885 --> 00:00:28.182
and Abakcus tells

00:00:27.994 --> 00:00:28.831
its story

00:00:29.358 --> 00:00:30.372
Full story on

00:00:30.183 --> 00:00:31.079
the dashboard
